good afternoon everyone  my name is dr miller and the scp we're  going to be looking at today  is scp 2009  object class ketter  special containment procedures samples  of scp-2009-2  are to be kept in refrigerated bsl for  compliance storage  at biosite 98. should an instance of  scp-2009-1 be required for testing or  interview purposes a single d-class  personnel is to be exposed to 3 grams  of scp-2009-2 following exposure  the affected individual is to be  contained in a bsl4  compliant containment cell for a period  of no less than 9 days  after which point it is to be treated as  a new instance of scp-2009-1  infection of d-class personnel with  scp-2092  is to take place only with the approval  of at least two on-site  level four personnel for the duration of  testing  the instance of scp-2009-1 is to be held  in a bsl4 compliant containment cell  kept at 10 degrees celsius humidity in  the cell of scp-2091  is to be kept at zero percent foundation  personnel are to wear level a hazmat  suits  when interacting with scp-2009-1 and  are to undergo full decontamination  following interaction  following completion of testing or  interaction the instance of scp-2091  is to be destroyed and its remains  incinerated  medical facilities news media and law  enforcement are to be monitored to  detect  uncontained instances of scp-2000  after confirmation and assessment of  scale mobile task force row 8  mushroom hunters is to be dispatched to  effect containment  description scp-2091 is the designation  for all instances of an anomalous male  humanoid  capable of asexual reproduction by means  of spores  instances of scp-2091 are genetically  identical  and prior to mutation display no unusual  physiology  instances of scp-2091 are fully sapient  and are capable of socializing normally  up until the point of production of  instances of scp-2009-2  instances of scp-2009-1 identify  themselves as thomas wang  no instance exhibits knowledge of its  anomalous properties  all instances also have a shared  baseline of memories  including childhood and early adulthood  taking place in the community  of pollensby california if exposed to  temperatures of more than 20 degrees  celsius  and humidity in excess of 40 for a  period in excess of five days  scp-2091 will seek out a darkened area  with preference given to tall buildings  and places adjacent  to high foot traffic areas the body of  scp-2091 will begin to distend and split  into thin  chitin-based hairs these hairs will be  used by scp-2091 to anchor itself to  nearby walls  objects and if possible draw limited  sustenance from them  scp-2091 will cease sapient activity  converting all of its energy to the  production of scp-2009-2  scp-2009-1 will continue the production  and release of scp-2009-2  until it eventually dies of exhaustion  scp-2009-2 is a microscopic spore  created by scp-2091 capable of infecting  human beings  during a typical period of production  scp-2091 is capable of producing  55 kilograms of scp-2092  instances of scp-2092 are airborne  and infect humans through the  respiratory system with three to four  days of exposure  individuals infected with scp-2009-2  will begin to experience symptoms of  nausea lethargy and  photosensitivity additionally  individuals will shun social contact  isolating themselves from others within  five to eight days the physiology of  affected individuals  will begin to change to match that of  scp-2009-1  the process can cause varying levels of  discomfort  proportional to the physiological  similarities between the individual  and scp-2091 affected individuals are  aware of the changes  and frequently exhibit extreme  psychological distress  during the process within eight to nine  days of exposure the physiology of the  subject will exactly match  that of scp-2009-1 as will its baseline  psychological state  dna and memories newly created instances  of scp-2091  exhibit no knowledge of their lives  prior to transformation  scp-2009 was discovered when reports of  a widespread infection  by a previously unknown disease in the  town  missouri were made to the center for  disease control on  1998 foundation agents embedded in the  initial response team reported extreme  psychological changes  brought on by exposure to scp-2009-2  in 46 of the town's residents the town  was immediately quarantined  with infected individuals being taken  into foundation custody  the cdc teams and the remainder of the  town's residents were isolated  until the nature of scp-2009 became  apparent  the town was destroyed and incinerated  under the cover story of freak wildfire  on 1998. the cdc teams and  uninfected residents were dosed with  class e amnestics  and released from foundation custody the  next day all but three of the newly  created instances of scp-2009-1  were destroyed and incinerated with the  rest used for purposes of testing and  the creation of instances of scp-2009-2  for purposes of study during the  destruction of the desiccated remains of  an instance of scp-2091  were found in the bell tower of first  methodist church  it is suspected that this instance was  the original vector  for scp-2009-1 although it is unknown  whether it was the original instance of  scp-2009-1  this is interview log 2009-7 m  13th of november 1999  playing log now interviewed  d 998 120 w abbreviated to d 998 by dr  amador  for conversational purposes an african  female  four days after exposure to scp-2009-2  interview took place in a darkened bsl4  compliant containment cell  hello d998 how are you feeling today  if you do not feel like cooperating d998  i can't turn the lights up  over i feel awful i feel like vomiting  and light hats everything nice what did  you give me  i'm sorry to hear that please describe  your earliest memory  if you would anyway if i answer  can you go away once you answer this  interview will be complete  yes okay i was five  for six my mother had to work late  and when she got in s